Typst math corpus — T51
======================

Each .typ file contains exactly one equation body. The first line is
// mode: display or // mode: inline; the rest, excluding its final LF, is the
source passed to typst_to_latex::convert and future compiler MathML tests.
Names/bodies 01–16 follow R4 §7, 17–26 follow R2 §5, and 27–36 follow math.md §10.
No writer.toml belongs in this directory or any fixture ancestor.

Pandoc records
--------------

Generated by an actual local run on 2026-10-28:

    pandoc 3.12.1
    Features: +server +lua

The equation body was wrapped as native Typst math according to its header:
display uses "$ " + body + " $\n"; inline uses "$" + body + "$\n".
The exact invocation was:

    pandoc -f typst -t latex --wrap=none

The native document was supplied on stdin. For example, 01-frac uses:

    printf '$ frac(a, b) $\n' | pandoc -f typst -t latex --wrap=none

The committed .pandoc.tex stores the mathematical BODY of that output: trim
surrounding output whitespace, require and remove the outer \[...\] or
\(...\) corresponding to the mode, remove only leading/trailing LF inside
those delimiters, and append exactly one final LF. Internal Pandoc spaces,
braces, commands and environment newlines are preserved, never hand-adjusted
to make Writer agree. 35-empty's oracle is one LF (an empty body).

33 files parsed. The following three actually failed with exit status 64 and
have no .pandoc.tex:

- 18-abs-norm-lr-mismatch: line 1, column 34, unexpected "$" (the mismatched
  lr(( a/b ]) case already recorded in R2).
- 29-unknown-fn: line 1, column 2, Identifier "foo" not found.
- 30-unknown-sym: line 1, column 2, Symbol does not have a method "reduce" or
  Symbol does not have variant "reduce".

The optional test reruns Pandoc when installed, checks its exact body bytes,
and checks those reader failures. No normal test requires Pandoc or runs Tylax.
Full original stdin/stdout/stderr/status records from preparation live in the
ignored task artifact pandoc-generation.json, not in the shipped fixture tree.

25-lr-floor-ceil preserves R2 x1's exact source, including escaped \| tokens.
This actual 3.12.1 run emits a literal |x| in its second term. R2's prose table
recorded \|x\| there; that older recording is NOT substituted for observed
output. Pinned typst-syntax parser.rs treats Escape as a leaf, while only the
actual delimiter token kinds enter math_delimited; the escaped bars therefore
do not justify changing Writer's actual-delimiter handling. The first lr term
retains Pandoc's invisible \left. and \right. wrappers.

Tylax records
-------------

Only 17–24 have .tylax.tex. They are transcribed from the pinned Tylax 0.3.8
outputs recorded in docs/research/R2-typst-syntax-subset.md §5.2, not regenerated.
The mapping is 17→R2 case7, 18→8, 19→9, 20→11, 21→12, 22→13, 23→14, 24→15.
R2 already removed its display delimiters; these files retain its recorded
body forms and append one LF. Tylax was never executed for this task.

Known errors/differences remain evidence: 20 uses the wrong \vec{1}{2}{3},
21 uses wide accents, and 24 uses numbered align rather than aligned. They
must not become the acceptance standard for Writer's mapped function table.

Writer comparisons
------------------

The mandatory Pandoc comparison covers 01–17 and 19–27. The only generic
normalization deletes whitespace, { and }. Each allowed semantic/form
difference is a reviewed (fixture, Pandoc form, Writer form, reason) tuple in
tests/typst_to_latex.rs. There are no whole-fixture exclusions beyond the
reader-failing 18, no generic command deletion, and no unreviewed substitutions.
New differences must be reviewed against math.md and the recorded source,
then added narrowly; an oracle bug does not change the converter contract.
